A $10.0\text{ cm}^3$ sample of $0.100\text{ mol dm}^{-3}$ aminoethanoic acid (glycine) was titrated with $0.100\text{ mol dm}^{-3}$ $\text{NaOH}$. After $20.0\text{ cm}^3$ of $\text{NaOH}$, an excess, had been added, the pH was found to be 12.5.

Using the following axes, sketch a graph showing how the pH changes during this titration.

{{figure:pdf_visual_01.png}}
